I think we can simplify the state here a bit. `manifestLists` and the new map are both tracking the manifest lists, so imo we can just keep the map, record the entry where `manifestLists.add` is today (paths are known before the write since `addMetadata` keeps the path), and store a `Set` since both consumers want one anyways. Something like:

```java
private final Map<String, Set<String>> manifestPathsByManifestList = Maps.newLinkedHashMap();

...

try (writer) {
  // keep track of the manifest lists created and the manifests they reference
  manifestPathsByManifestList.put(
      manifestList.location(),
      manifests.stream().map(ManifestFile::path).collect(Collectors.toSet()));
  ...
  writer.addAll(Arrays.asList(manifestFiles));
}
```

then cleanup just iterates over `keySet()`:

```java
